  "status": "Three scoped Lean-checked gates after the Banks/Siegel determinant review; no new independent RH arithmetic estimate.",
  "paper_inspiration": {
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2610.15483v1",
    "mechanism": "One nonzero common integral determinant subjected to lower-weight Frobenius row operations at many primes.",
    "imported_or_formally_verified": false
  },
  "gates": [
    {
      "name": "literal masked Frobenius",
      "proved": [
        "p=2 cutoff original determinant -7, replacement -4, boundary -3; lower masked correction not in earlier rational row span.",
        "p=3 cutoff original -116, replacement -108, replacement row divisible by 3.",
        "Finite masked-flag repairs preserve determinants 1 and 2."
      ],
      "scope": "Pointwise congruence alone does not imply determinant invariance after these literal cutoffs. Not all cutoff-compatible determinants."
    },
    {
      "name": "arbitrary finite interval-cell closure",
      "proved": [
        "For unequal and growing interval cells, the common masked polynomial-flag determinant equals the product of their superfactorials.",
        "Cell translations do not change the determinant.",
        "The factorial row normalization accounts for its entire integer value."
      ],
      "scope": "This complete interval-block repair only; non-block evaluation spaces remain open."
    },
    {
      "name": "adjacent Pascal minor",
      "proved": [
        "Actual determinant is positive and D*(k+1)=choose(k+t,k)*choose(k+t+1,k).",
        "Exact six-factorial identity.",
        "At every denominator, the literal layer equals two original binomial carries minus the divisor indicator of k+1.",
        "For arbitrary weights the extra channel is exactly an endpoint divisor sum.",
        "With all prime powers and unit phase retained its norm is <=log X and its X^(-beta) normalization tends to zero for every beta>0 along X=2^(2J)."
      ],
      "scope": "Only the additional minor channel is paid. Both original signed carry packets and any unestimated exterior row mass remain unpaid."
    }
  ],
  "information_loss_guards": [
    "A base-prime-coded total valuation, a consecutive divisibility tower, and literal carry layers are different observables.",
    "choose(4,2) has binary valuation 1 but the actual carry occurs at order 2; the Lean regression retains that location.",
    "Determinant subtraction can produce prime factors beyond the entry cutoff: [[1,1],[1,6]] has determinant 5.",
    "Never combine prime divisibilities of different prime-dependent determinants."
  ],
  "paper_level_only": [
    "General bounded-gap Pascal minor formula with polynomial factor Q_ab; no generic literal phase theorem claimed.",
    "Fixed-gap base-prime residual O(log X); no growing-row aggregate source estimate claimed."
  ],
